WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.460
Jai Shri Mataji, greetings to everyone.

2
00:00:04.290 --> 00:00:10.510
I would like to share some new things we have on the translation portal.

3
00:00:12.770 --> 00:00:15.250
There are three pieces of news today.

4
00:00:16.350 --> 00:00:23.240
First of all, there is now a button in the top right corner: "Settings".

5
00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:29.670
Before, there were several buttons in its place: switching the language

6
00:00:29.670 --> 00:00:32.970
and the theme. Now they are tucked away here.

7
00:00:33.070 --> 00:00:39.220
If we click it, we see that the "Interface language" can now be switched here.

8
00:00:43.650 --> 00:00:48.490
And "Expert mode". It used to be at the very bottom of the page; now it is here too,

9
00:00:48.490 --> 00:00:55.380
as an option. As a reminder, "Expert mode" lets you see not only what

10
00:00:55.380 --> 00:01:01.880
needs work and what you are working on, but also what has already been done

11
00:01:01.980 --> 00:01:08.780
and approved, and also what is waiting for some technical attention

12
00:01:08.900 --> 00:01:12.440
before a translator can take it on.

13
00:01:16.420 --> 00:01:21.180
Second: now, when we go into

14
00:01:21.850 --> 00:01:28.300
editing, non-Ukrainian characters, such

15
00:01:28.300 --> 00:01:34.550
as English-style quotation marks, the apostrophe and so on,

16
00:01:34.550 --> 00:01:41.070
automatically, because this clearly needs converting if it is a Ukrainian

17
00:01:41.070 --> 00:01:43.970
piece of text, get converted.

18
00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:45.610
Let's take an example.

19
00:01:45.610 --> 00:01:52.360
I have just switched my keyboard to English and I type a single apostrophe,

20
00:01:52.360 --> 00:01:56.860
an English one. It is automatically typed as a Ukrainian one.

21
00:01:57.060 --> 00:02:02.920
The same with quotation marks: however you type them, automatically, English ones,

22
00:02:03.320 --> 00:02:09.500
Latin ones, from the English layout, they are automatically turned into «yalynky».

23
00:02:09.840 --> 00:02:16.380
The same with dashes. If we put a hyphen between words, like here, you see, it

24
00:02:16.380 --> 00:02:22.500
is converted automatically. Also, if we accidentally typed several spaces,

25
00:02:24.060 --> 00:02:27.360
then when we finish editing

26
00:02:28.380 --> 00:02:30.900
they were automatically turned into single ones.

27
00:02:33.590 --> 00:02:37.030
So these are the automatic corrections.

28
00:02:37.950 --> 00:02:44.530
What else? This is the third interesting point: now you can

29
00:02:45.070 --> 00:02:47.470
turn on "Highlight typos".

30
00:02:49.680 --> 00:02:56.220
Let me first show where this came from, why do this at all.

31
00:02:56.220 --> 00:03:03.020
First, it is very easy to make a typo, and then

32
00:03:03.020 --> 00:03:09.880
someone at the next stage, a machine or a person, will find the typo and fix it.

33
00:03:11.100 --> 00:03:12.920
But suppose

34
00:03:14.090 --> 00:03:20.830
the editor, the translator, would like to see this mistake themselves rather than leave

35
00:03:20.830 --> 00:03:26.710
it to the next stage. For that you can turn on "Highlight typos".

36
00:03:27.280 --> 00:03:31.900
And thanks to that we get this red highlighting.

37
00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:38.940
If you see it, just reread the word once more

38
00:03:38.940 --> 00:03:41.250
to check it for typos.

39
00:03:42.530 --> 00:03:49.290
And now the second part of this highlighting. Let's turn it

40
00:03:49.290 --> 00:03:56.190
off for now, and I'll show how this can happen. Let's remove this. For example, here I came in,

41
00:03:56.190 --> 00:04:02.430
and I have the English layout. I see that in the original we have Sahaja Yoga with a capital

42
00:04:02.430 --> 00:04:07.860
letter. I immediately take the capital letter and correct it.

43
00:04:08.500 --> 00:04:11.380
And here it means the layout is wrong.

44
00:04:11.380 --> 00:04:17.410
I switch over, but I forget about this one letter, and it is actually a Latin one.

45
00:04:18.120 --> 00:04:24.650
If we have "Highlight typos" turned on, then not only

46
00:04:24.650 --> 00:04:31.360
words that don't match the dictionaries get highlighted, but also places where

47
00:04:31.360 --> 00:04:36.760
layouts got mixed, and it even tells you what it highlights, and writes it out.

48
00:04:39.210 --> 00:04:42.550
This way we can go ahead and fix it.

49
00:04:47.130 --> 00:04:51.480
Why is this feature hidden behind a separate checkbox?

50
00:04:51.620 --> 00:04:57.240
It needs some memory on the device, because it has to load the dictionaries

51
00:04:57.660 --> 00:04:59.780
of the Ukrainian language,

52
00:05:00.820 --> 00:05:06.620
and also a Sahaja dictionary, to work out which word is acceptable,

53
00:05:06.640 --> 00:05:12.220
in use, and which one contains a typo.

54
00:05:12.760 --> 00:05:19.550
So please do try turning it on, but on some very

55
00:05:19.550 --> 00:05:25.110
old devices with very little memory it may either not work or work

56
00:05:25.110 --> 00:05:29.750
slowly, which is exactly why it was made a separate option.

57
00:05:32.670 --> 00:05:39.490
On normal devices you can turn it on, but if on your device it does not

58
00:05:39.490 --> 00:05:40.490
work,

59
00:05:41.470 --> 00:05:46.770
then don't turn it on, and please let us know.

60
00:05:46.830 --> 00:05:51.970
If such a device turns up, we'll try to make it so that on older devices too

61
00:05:51.970 --> 00:05:58.930
it works. I don't have such devices, so I cannot confirm whether there is

62
00:05:58.930 --> 00:05:59.930
such a problem.
